<title>USA: Sherwin-Williams Q4 shr $0.45 vs $0.39.</title>
<headline>Sherwin-Williams Q4 shr $0.45 vs $0.39.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sherwin-Williams Co and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>			   Three months ended  Twelve months ended</p>
<p>				December 31,	  December 31,</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p>Thousands of dollars,</p>
<p>except per share data.</p>
<p> Net sales	 $958,844    $740,907  $4,132,879  $3,273,819</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>Operating expenses</p>
<p>			871,586     680,987   3,714,264   2,952,525</p>
<p>Interest expense</p>
<p>			  5,521	   711	24,537	 2,532</p>
<p>Interest and net</p>
<p>investment income</p>
<p>			(1,982)     (3,895)     (6,819)    (11,518)</p>
<p>   Other	     19,891	 9,508	25,520	11,782</p>
<p>     Total	  895,016     687,311   3,757,502   2,955,321</p>
<p>Income before income</p>
<p>   taxes	     63,828	53,596     375,377     318,498</p>
<p> Income taxes	24,716	19,830     146,220     117,844</p>
<p> Net income	  39,112	33,766     229,157     200,654</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>			   0.45	  0.39	  2.65	  2.34</p>
<p>Avg shrs	 86,725,048  85,854,147  86,450,388  85,743,273</p>
<p>Note: The financial results for the three months and twelve months ended Dec. 31, 1996 include the results of operations of Pratt &amp; Lambert United, Inc., acquired during January 1996, and other smaller acquisitions acquired at various times during 1996.</p>
<p>Excluding the results of operations of these acquisitions and the related costs of financing the purchases from the fourth quarter of 1996, sales increased 8.3 percent and net income increased 14.1 percent over 1995's fourth quarter.</p>
<p>For the twelve months ended Dec. 31, 1996 excluding acquisitions, sales increased 7.5 percent and net income increased 12.6 percent.</p>
<p>On January 29, 1997, the Company's board of directors authorized a two-for-one split of the common stock effected in the form of a 100 percent stock dividend to be distributed on or about March 28, 1997, to holders of record on March 3, 1997. The average shares and per share amounts shown above have not been restated to reflect this stock split.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
